# Task 1 - word count, ignoring case.
#
# Write three functions and hand them to a job. You choose the names, the
# parameters and the types: nothing is inferred, and no function is a
# mapper because of what it is called. A function is accepted in a
# position only if its signature fits that position.
#
# What a pair should be, and what "ignoring case" implies about when to
# normalise, are yours to decide. Press ctrl/cmd + K for the reference.

@mapper
class Worker:
    pass

@reducer
class Collector:
    pass

m1 = Worker(speed=1.0)
m2 = Worker(speed=1.0)
m3 = Worker(speed=1.0)
r1 = Collector(speed=1.0)
r2 = Collector(speed=1.0)

world = World(machines=[m1, m2, m3, r1, r2])

# --- your code -------------------------------------------------------
# Write the three functions here, then run the job in the world:
#
#     job = MapReduce(map=..., reduce=..., partition=...)
#     world.run(job)
